-- title:
--   Adeles generating the unit ideal recombine via orthogonal idempotents
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, written as a field $K$ carrying a `NumberField` instance, and let $\mathbb{A}_K =$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K` be its adele ring, formed with respect to the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$. Let $\iota$ be a finite index type and let $t : \iota \to \mathbb{A}_K$ be a family of adeles indexed by $\iota$. Assume that the ideal of $\mathbb{A}_K$ generated by the set of values of $t$ is the whole ring, i.e. `Ideal.span (Set.range t) = ⊤`; equivalently, there are adeles $c_i$ with $\sum_i c_i t_i = 1$. The assertion is that there exists a family $e : \iota \to \mathbb{A}_K$ which is a complete family of orthogonal idempotents in the sense of Mathlib's `CompleteOrthogonalIdempotents` — each $e_i$ satisfies $e_i^2 = e_i$, one has $e_i e_j = 0$ for $i \neq j$, and $\sum_{i} e_i = 1$ — such that the single element $\sum_{i} e_i t_i$ is a unit of $\mathbb{A}_K$, that is, an idele. Note that the idempotents are produced, not given, and that no relation between $e$ and the coefficients witnessing the hypothesis is asserted.
--
--   This is the finitely generated form of the exchange property for the adele ring of a number field, in the sense of Warfield and Nicholson: a finite family of adeles generating the unit ideal can be recombined, using a complete orthogonal decomposition of $1$, into a single invertible adele. It is used in the analysis of $\sigma$-conjugacy of adelic matrices of rank two, namely by [`AutomorphicForm.isSigmaConjugate_adeleRing_of_normString_eq_of_normString_mem_center_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.isSigmaConjugate_adeleRing_of_normString_eq_of_normString_mem_center_of_finrank_eq_two).
